<Project>
  <!--
    Deliberately empty. This file exists to SUPPRESS the default merge that ships inside
    ILRepack.Lib.MSBuild.Task, not to add anything.

    That package's build targets declare their own target:

        <Target Name="ILRepack" AfterTargets="Build"
                Condition="$(Configuration.Contains('Release')) and !Exists('$(ILRepackTargetsFile)')">

    with $(ILRepackTargetsFile) defaulting to $(ProjectDir)ILRepack.targets — this file. Because
    the condition is keyed on the configuration name, it fires in Release only, which is why the
    problem was invisible in Debug.

    Left to run it merges $(OutputPath)*.dll indiscriminately and passes NO LibraryPath, so
    Mono.Cecil cannot resolve the host assemblies the merged deps reference and the build fails
    with "Failed to resolve assembly: 'Grasshopper, Version=8.24.25281.15001'". Our own RepackGha
    target (in Physalia.GH.csproj) runs first and does the merge properly — correct denylist,
    LibraryPath derived from the resolved @(ReferencePath) — so the .gha it produced was already
    correct and the failure came entirely from this second, unconfigured pass running on top of it.

    Its companion CleanReferenceCopyLocalPaths target is gated on the same condition and would
    delete every ReferenceCopyLocalPath from the output — including the JSON stack that RepackGha
    deliberately keeps LOOSE and unmerged (see the RepackDenyList comments). Suppressing the pair
    is what keeps those DLLs beside the .gha.
  -->
</Project>
